{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>All the days of the poor</b> — it is a description, and it refers to the one who is distressed." "<b>Feast</b> — lacking a kaf. The meaning: poor in mind and in money — his days are evil; the opposite of a glad heart and a good and joyful heart — at a feast always, that is, like a dog eating and drinking and rejoicing every day."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:58.647286970Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}